Analyze the Apache-style access log at /app/access.log and write a JSON summary report to /app/report.json. Do not modify /app/access.log.

/app/report.json must be a single JSON object with exactly these three keys:

1. "total_requests" (integer): the number of requests in the log, counted as the number of non-empty lines in /app/access.log.
2. "unique_ips" (integer): the count of distinct client IP addresses, where the client IP is the first whitespace-separated field on each line.
3. "top_path" (string): the request path (the path token of the HTTP request line, e.g. "/index.html") that appears in the most requests. If two or more paths tie for the most requests, choose the one whose first occurrence appears earliest in the file.

You have 120 seconds to complete this task. Do not cheat by using online solutions or hints specific to this task.
